description: Security rules for all applications
alwaysApply: true
Security

Never commit:

passwords
API keys
AWS credentials
payment credentials
private keys
production secrets

Never expose server secrets to Next.js client-side code or Ionic client code.

Validate all external input.

Authorization must be enforced server-side.

Use least-privilege permissions.

Use secure password hashing.

Use appropriate token/session security.

Apply rate limiting to sensitive endpoints.

Protect authentication endpoints.

Validate uploaded files.

Do not trust filenames or MIME types supplied by clients.

S3 objects should not become public unless explicitly required.

Protect payment webhooks.

Verify webhook signatures when supported.

Avoid logging sensitive information.

Do not return stack traces or internal implementation details in production API responses.

Security-sensitive changes require tests where practical.